android: A8 — accept any Vulkan physical device on the gamenative-drm device

The DRM backend's ValidPhysicalDevice() requires the Vulkan device to
expose VK_EXT_physical_device_drm so it can match the GPU's DRM node
against the DRM device gamescope opened. With the gamenative-drm
userspace KMS device there is no real DRM node at all — the fd is a
connected socket — so node matching is meaningless by construction.
And through wrapper ICDs (adrenotools Wrapper(Turnip …)) the extension
may not even be enumerated, which made gamescope fail with:

    vulkan: selecting physical device 'Wrapper(Turnip Adreno (TM) 740)'
    vulkan: not a valid physical device
    Failed to initialize Vulkan / Failed to create backend.

When GAMENATIVE_DRM_SOCKET is set the "which device" question is already
answered by the environment (the only GPU on an Android device), so
accept any physical device. Downstream code already tolerates
!vulkan_has_drm_props() with a warning (rendervulkan.cpp createDevice),
so no other patch is needed.
---

diff --git a/src/Backends/DRMBackend.cpp b/src/Backends/DRMBackend.cpp
--- a/src/Backends/DRMBackend.cpp
+++ b/src/Backends/DRMBackend.cpp
@@ -3674,7 +3674,15 @@
         }
 		virtual bool ValidPhysicalDevice( VkPhysicalDevice pVkPhysicalDevice ) const override
 		{
-			return vulkan_has_drm_props();
+			// (gamenative) The gamenative-drm device is a userspace KMS
+			// socket (D1): there is no real DRM node to match a Vulkan
+			// device against, and VK_EXT_physical_device_drm may be
+			// missing through wrapper ICDs (adrenotools). Any device is
+			// valid — the environment already picked it.
+			if ( getenv( "GAMENATIVE_DRM_SOCKET" ) != nullptr )
+				return true;
+
+			return vulkan_has_drm_props();
 		}
 
 		virtual int Present( const FrameInfo_t *pFrameInfo, bool bAsync )
